#!/rom/bin/angel
// Lesson 1: Hello!
//
// Welcome to the guide. Each lesson is a small program, and you're reading one now. The lines
// starting with // are comments: the computer skips them, so they're where the lesson talks to
// you. The other lines are the program.
//
// Press F5 to run it. What it prints appears in the Output below.
//
// How the guide works:
//   - Read a lesson from top to bottom, then press F5 and see what it does.
//   - At the end there are things to try. Change the program and press F5 again. The lesson
//     itself can't be changed where it is, so the first F5 after a change asks where to save
//     your copy (your scripts folder is a good place).
//   - Put the cursor on a word such as println and press F1: the Help tab says what it does.
//   - The next lesson is in Help > Guide.

println("Hello!");

// println writes what's between the brackets, then starts a new line. Text in a program goes
// between double quotes: "like this". That's called a string.
println("My name is Angel. I'm a computer program.");

// print does the same without starting a new line, so the next thing follows on.
print("One, ");
print("two, ");
println("three!");

// println() with nothing in the brackets just ends the line: an empty line.
println();

// The program runs from the top line to the bottom one, in order.
println("This is the last line. Bye!");

// Try this:
//   1. Change "Hello!" to say hello to you, by name. Press F5.
//   2. Add a line that prints your favourite food.
//   3. What happens if you take away a semicolon (;) at the end of a line? Look for the red
//      wavy line, and the message in the Problems tab. Put it back.
